        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Caldwell%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough was officially incorporated on March 31, 1898, after separating from the larger Caldwell Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Caldwell%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1702 settlers bought 14,000 acres from the Lenape for goods worth $325, marking the first formal claim in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Caldwell%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1740s Horse Neck Riots were among the earliest American challenges to Royal authority, sparked by local settlers’ grievances.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
